   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Development Project - Pastoral Land Commission, Rond&#xF4;nia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project in the Western state of Rond&#xF4;nia located in the Amazon works to build the technical and practical capacity of rural families to manage their land - through experimentation and the application of agro-ecological practices and methods. The families receive training from specialist technicians in environmentally sustainable farming techniques. Their land is assessed and following meetings between families and technicians work begins to increase their agricultural production with the final aim of making them self-sufficient. The focus is on families working together because this will lay foundations for collective planning and production, thus strengthening the sustainable livelihoods of the entire community. 

The project also involves setting up an &quot;information bank&quot; which will provide both agricultural technicians and rural families with information on the research and practice of agro-ecological techniques, and in addition a &quot;seed bank&quot; that will protect and preserve the biodiversity of the region and promote the use of local natural resources.</narrative>
  </description>
